    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green (2/2, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation on the owner resource with minimal structural impact.\n\n**Change:** Owners returned from `GET /api/owners/{id}` (and the create response) now carry a `locality` field derived from the city \u2014 `Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, and `UNKNOWN` for any other city.\n\n**Files touched (3):**\n1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n2. `mapper/Localities.java` (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive helper holding the fixed city\u2192region table and a single `regionOf(city)` lookup (defaults to `UNKNOWN`), mirroring the existing `CityCodes`/`Namesakes`/`Households` helper pattern.\n3. `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `Localities.regionOf(owner.getCity())`, consistent with the other derived-field expressions already there.\n\nThe derivation lives in its own tiny class rather than growing the mapper or a controller method, keeping every changed function simple and its surrounding complexity low.",
